-- Type inference (D007): the canonical example. `myId = id` has no signature;
-- `id` has the fixed type `A -> A`, so `myId : A -> A` is inferred (NOT
-- specialized to a narrower type — D007 forbids signature specialization, but
-- composition/usage still determines the concrete type at each use site).
--
--   `myId`  : A -> A          (inferred from `id`)
--   `myId 0`: Int             (A determined = Int by applying to the literal)
--   `main`  : Eff Unit Unit   (inferred)
--
-- Expected: exit code 0
-- D072: the principal-type oracle infers the SCHEMA `a -> a` for the
-- sig-less `myId = id` and routes it to the telescope (PolyFunInfo);
-- the use `myId 0` instantiates it at `Int -> Int` in check mode and
-- the kernel validates the instantiation (check-after-infer).

import I.Linux.Syscalls as S

myId = id

main = exit@S (myId 0)
